tegrated the iOS camera module into the main repo as `camera_apple`, but the documentation still referenced the old godot-ios-plugins requirement, and several features from #106305 / godot-ios-plugins#89 were not yet ported.\r\n\r\n- Fix outdated docs that still referenced godot-ios-plugins for iOS camera support.\r\n- Port screen rotation handling that accounts for front/back camera differences.\r\n- Port initial orientation detection when feeds are discovered.\r\n- Stop camera capture on background transition and restore on foreground.\r\n- Handle pixel buffer row stride to prevent data corruption on padded buffers.\r\n- Track device lock state and properly unlock on deactivation.\r\n- Validate capture session inputs/outputs before adding, with proper cleanup on failure.\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097519,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc1MTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:ios","name":"platform:ios","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097780,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc3ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:macos","name":"platform:macos","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platforms","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":14236899,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A2Tzj","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/24","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godo